  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"0.3.0\"\n  llvm_modern_commit: 3cbe75b1433a90a28db068d700b7effd2de8f401\n\npackage:\n  name: numba-cuda-mlir\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  - url: https://github.com/NVIDIA/numba-cuda-mlir/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n    sha256: c015e5c07f17d924e13aa62a64940f53c85c53ce1f2d4e1c587d50ce21023d0c\n    target_directory: src\n  - url: https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/archive/${{ llvm_modern_commit }}.tar.gz\n    sha256: a2d6587b0793f7f6fb21c4607e6d86cd40377686f58162fbae5e206d2e24dfe2\n    target_directory: llvm-modern-src\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  skip:\n    - not linux\n    - match(python, \"<3.11\")\n    - match(python, \">=3.12\")\n    - cuda_compiler_version != \"None\"\n  script:\n    file: build.sh\n    env:\n      NUMBA_CUDA_MLIR_VERSION: ${{ version }}\n  # The CUDA runtime libraries (cudart, nvrtc, nvjitlink, nvvm) are dlopen'd at\n  # runtime, not link time linked, and the bundled libLLVM-7.so / MLIR C-API .so\n  # are loaded dynamically, exempt them from the link checks.\n  dynamic_linking:\n    overdepending_behavior: ignore\n    missing_dso_allowlist:\n      - '*/libLLVM-7.so'\n      - '*/libMLIRPythonCAPI.so'\n      - '*/libMLIRPythonSupport-numba_cuda_mlir.so'\n\nrequirements:\n  ignore_run_exports:\n    by_name:\n      - cuda-cudart\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - cmake >=3.24\n    - ninja\n    - make\n    - git\n  host:\n    - python\n    - pip\n    - setuptools >=64\n    - wheel\n    # Build deps for the modern LLVM/MLIR Python bindings:\n    - numpy\n    - pybind11\n    # nanobind >2.13 breaks numba-cuda-mlir's MLIR bindings\n    - nanobind >=2.9,<2.13\n    - typing-extensions\n    - dlpack\n    # zlib + zstd: modern LLVM/MLIR links both for compression, so the bundled\n    # libMLIRPythonCAPI.so needs them at build and run time.\n    - zlib\n    - zstd\n    # CUDA headers only (no nvcc). numba-cuda-mlir handles CUDA ABI compat at\n    # runtime, so the build-time CUDA version is not significant. NVRTC/nvJitLink\n    # headers aren't needed at build time (those libraries are dlopen'd).\n    - cuda-version 13.*\n    - cuda-cudart-dev\n    - cuda-driver-dev\n    - cuda-crt-dev_${{ target_platform }}\n    - cuda-cccl\n    - libllvm7.1\n  run:\n    - python\n    - numpy\n    - llvmlite\n    - if: match(python, \"<3.12\")\n      then: typing-extensions\n    - zstd\n    - packaging\n    - cuda-version >=12.2,<14.0.0a0\n    - cuda-cudart\n    - cuda-nvrtc\n    - libnvjitlink >=12.3.0\n    - cuda-nvvm-impl\n    - cuda-cccl\n    - cuda-bindings\n    - cuda-core >=0.5.1,<2.0.0\n    - libllvm7.1\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - numba_cuda_mlir\n        - numba_cuda_mlir._mlir.ir\n      pip_check: true\n  - script:\n      - python -c \"import numba_cuda_mlir; from numba_cuda_mlir import cuda\"\n      # Confirm the bundled native libraries are present and located.\n      - python -c \"import numba_cuda_mlir._mlir._mlir_libs as L, os; assert os.path.exists(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(L.__file__), 'libMLIRPythonCAPI.so'))\"\n      - python -c \"import numba_cuda_mlir, os; assert os.path.exists(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(numba_cuda_mlir.__file__), 'lib', 'libLLVM-7.so'))\"\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/NVIDIA/numba-cuda-mlir\n  license: Apache-2.0 AND Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception AND NCSA\n  license_file:\n    - src/LICENSE\n    - src/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES\n  summary: numba-cuda-mlir Python Compiler (MLIR/LLVM CUDA kernel backend)\n  repository: https://github.com/NVIDIA/numba-cuda-mlir\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - conda-forge/cuda-python\n    - brandon-b-miller\n",
